<h2>A genuinely diversified market</h2>
<p>Unlike some of our single-commodity-dominated lanes, Malaysia takes a real spread of Indian agricultural products — onion, groundnut, spices and more — which reflects both direct culinary demand and Malaysia's position as a Southeast Asian food-processing and re-distribution centre.</p>

<h2>Halal certification: confirm the specifics with your importer</h2>
<p>Malaysia's majority-Muslim population means halal certification is a live consideration for many food categories. We don't hold or claim halal certification ourselves — what we do is arrange documentation to match whatever certifying body your importer specifies, and we'd rather have that conversation at the enquiry stage than after a shipment is ready to load.</p>

<h2>Onion supply is subject to the same Indian policy caveats as elsewhere</h2>
<p>As with any Malaysian order involving Indian onion, pricing and terms reflect current Indian export-policy conditions (minimum export price, any applicable duty) confirmed at the time of order — not a fixed quote assuming settled policy. See our <a href="/products/fresh-vegetables/red-onion/">red onion page</a> for the full explanation.</p>

